<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates continue to rise in wary mkt.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates continue to rise in wary mkt.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) climbed further on Monday in line with an expected tightness in the market, traders said.</p>
<p>The central bank anticipating such an event had raised its overnight lending rate by four percentage points to 26 percent, they said.</p>
<p>Banks increased their swap rates late last week when the central bank raised liquidity reserves by two percentage points to mop up pesos that may be shifted to currency speculation.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  AUG 4		 AUG 1</p>
<p>    1 W		25  1/2		 24  1/16</p>
<p>    2 W		25  3/8		 24</p>
<p>    1 M		24  7/8		 23</p>
<p>    2 M		23  5/8		 21 13/16</p>
<p>    3 M		22  1/8		 20 11/16</p>
<p>    6 M		19  9/16		18  5/8</p>
<p>    12M		17  3/4		 17  1/8</p>
<p>    VAL		5-Aug		   4-Aug</p>
